<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hungarian Diet</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hungarian Diet was the parliament of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Compromise of 1867</a> it governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>'s internal affairs within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Dual Monarchy</a>, while sharing foreign policy, defence and related finance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. Dominated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyar</a> elite, it was a central institution in the governance of the Austro-Hungarian Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hungarian-diet.jpg" alt="Hungarian Diet" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_Assembly_of_Hungary_(1830).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
